Start a new monitor at normal size when its zoom-in is disabled

onConnect warps the monitorAdded zoom to 0, and onPresented keeps it there
for 5 frames before animating it to 1, so that the zoom-in is not lost to a
modeset. With the animation disabled, by its leaf or by
animations:enabled = false, those 5 frames are still drawn magnified 2x,
then the monitor jumps to normal size.

Start at 1, past the 5-frame buffer, when the zoom-in would not animate.

Not yet upstream.

--- a/src/output/Monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
@@ -117,8 +117,12 @@ void CMonitor::onConnect(bool noRule) {
     Event::bus()->m_events.monitor.preAdded.emit(m_self.lock());
     CScopeGuard x = {[]() { State::monitorLayoutController()->arrange(); }};
 
-    m_zoomAnimProgress->setValueAndWarp(0.F);
-    m_zoomAnimFrameCounter = 0;
+    // With monitorAdded or all animations disabled, start at normal size: the 5-frame buffer
+    // in onPresented only delays the zoom-in, and would otherwise draw 5 frames magnified.
+    static auto PANIMENABLED = CConfigValue<Config::INTEGER>("animations:enabled");
+    const bool  ZOOMIN       = *PANIMENABLED && m_zoomAnimProgress->enabled();
+    m_zoomAnimProgress->setValueAndWarp(ZOOMIN ? 0.F : 1.F);
+    m_zoomAnimFrameCounter = ZOOMIN ? 0 : 5;
 
     g_pEventLoopManager->doLater([] {
         State::Workspace::placementController()->ensurePersistentWorkspacesPresent(
